{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1100876-a-peace-treaty-with-the-fera","id":1100876,"title":"A peace treaty with the Fera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-06T10:16:58-07:00","id":1100876,"title":"A peace treaty with the Fera","content":"I was thinking about doing a game where the North American Garou attempt to make a peace treaty with the Fera. I'm just spitballing the idea now but it would be arranged around a moot and there would be mostly roleplaying done there (albeit maybe a few challenges or duels). I'm curious if anyone has any ideas what might be addressed during this or challenges to face in such an endeavor.<br /> <br /> Which Fera would be for, which would be against, and who would try to sabotage it.<br /> <br /> Ditto Garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T10:47:51-07:00","id":1100884,"title":"","content":"The Uktena, Wendigo, Qualmi, Corax, &amp; Nuwashi are already known for having long standing relations with one another in NA. You have Gurahl and Mokole who are present and would offer assistance but the other tribes make this complicated. When the Three Brothers were the only tribes in the area they all cohabited just fine. Now all of the relationships with the Garou are excessively strained.<br /> <br /> Challenges include getting the Nuwashi, Gurahl, and/or Mokole to even trust an alliance that included the Garou Nation. 2 or the 3 don't even want the Garou to know they are still alive and the third has lost all hope for the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T10:48:57-07:00","id":1100885,"title":"","content":"It is hard to do &quot;treaties&quot; on this scale because there is no formal organization that can represent the whole Garou Nation and enforce any such policy among all the individual septs and Garou, likewise for the multiple groups of Fera.<br /> <br /> At best there could be a grand concolation where tribal elders of all the tribes in North America get together and agree for a common policy towards the Fera, and they announce at a caern there will be a concolation in three months to discuss that. Then those elders from all the tribes would send messengers throughout North America to convince all the other important Garou to attend. It would take a lot of politicking to assemble sufficient elders and sept leaders so that the moot's decisions would be accepted and upheld throughout the entire North American continent. But even then, there will be Garou who will not attend; Garou who will not agree; and enforcement of any provisions will depend on individual Garou at individual septs to do so.<br /> <br /> Presumably you already have a reason for why elder Garou of each tribe are doing this - some kind of crisis or prophecy to provoke this. And it's very unclear to me what such a &quot;peace treaty&quot; would mean in practical terms.<br /> <br /> As for the Fera, there are two groups closest to the Garou who would most likely support them - the Corax and Nuwisha.<br /> <br /> Then there are groups who would be more problematic because they don't trust the Garou - the Gurahl and the North American Bastet (Balam, Pumonca, and Qualmi). However, their overall agenda is probably close enough that there is opportunity for dialogue and diplomacy.<br /> <br /> Next are groups whose agendas I think are too different for them to care about making deals with the Garou - Ananasi and Ratkin.<br /> <br /> There are also groups which probably don't live in North America or considered lost and therefore don't care and are out of scope - Ajaba, the other Bastet (Bagheera, Bubasti, Ceilican, Khan, Simba, and Swara), Kitsune, Nagah, and Rokea. I'm unsure about the Mokole because of North American alligators.<br /> <br /> But for any of the Fera, they probably have even greater problems than the Garou about obtaining some kind of group consensus and authority to entreat with these elder Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:58:13-07:00","id":1100907,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by peace treaty? Do you mean something like a NA Ahdi/Emerald Courts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T12:19:21-07:00","id":1100918,"title":"","content":"I think that it should happen given the threats that the Fera (including the Garou) face during the 21st century. A Western Alliance against the common enemies of the Fera could be frighteningly effective, which is probably why the agents of the Weaver and the Wyrm would move Heaven and Earth to try to prevent it from occurring. Of course, it would require the Western Garou to apologize to the Western Fera, which might be only slightly less difficult than preventing the Apocalypse, but it is likely the only way that the Apocalypse could be prevented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T13:24:36-07:00","id":1100940,"title":"","content":"So I did a similar arch as the point in a friend's campaign. The Mokole can definitely be in North America due to both American Alligators (Halpatee) and American Crocodile (Piasa), Gila Monster (Unktehi), and some caiman (Syrta) species are located in Mexico.<br /> <br /> I played on an idea from the breed book involving Mokole still following Turtle as a totem, and having the 1 pt merit &quot;Memory of the Lost Ones&quot; only instead of extinct fera breeds (like the Apis) I gave him memories of the Croatan. This Character was able to interplay with the rest of the party and allowed for the Mokole to be involved in this new peace group (We called it the Shifter Confederation of the Americas....as a joke as some of our group were members of the SCA). The fun was playing this alliance among the players (Nuwisha, Mokole, Corax, and Garou) and having the issues as a go between between the breeds. It might not be for everyone, but its some ideas I thought some may like to kick around.<br /> <br /> We also created a turtle varna before the Ao were a thing, because we really liked the idea of driving the &quot;turtle&quot; theme (like turtle island) and its importance home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 06-06-2017, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T14:31:46-07:00","id":1100964,"title":"","content":"An alternative Turtle Varna that could physically enter the High Umbra to defend and to manage the Mnesis would have been interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T14:40:40-07:00","id":1100968,"title":"","content":"My idea is the treaty for the Fera is Albretch trying to do reconcilliation for the North American Garou with the Fera so they can stop fighting each other and work together to share information so can focus more on fighting the Wyrm. Even this really low amount of business is only because of a crisis in the setting (my Under a Blood Red Moon campaign) and also because of the Stargazers leaving.<br /> <br /> It's going to have a lot of really bad fallout but is only about the North American branch as the Eastern Fera don't have to make such an agreement since they did so already with the Stargazers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T15:04:15-07:00","id":1100974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1100876-a-peace-treaty-with-the-fera?p=1100968#post1100968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea is the treaty for the Fera is Albretch trying to do reconcilliation for the North American Garou with the Fera so they can stop fighting each other and work together to share information so can focus more on fighting the Wyrm. Even this really low amount of business is only because of a crisis in the setting (my Under a Blood Red Moon campaign) and also because of the Stargazers leaving.<br /> <br /> It's going to have a lot of really bad fallout but is only about the North American branch as the Eastern Fera don't have to make such an agreement since they did so already with the Stargazers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are Kitsune in the Ahdi Kitsune go where Kitsune go.<br /> <br /> <br /> More seriously rather than a vague &quot;everyone fights together against problems&quot;(which seems to generally have been the case in places like the Amazon) what are the specifics? What are the Garou offering for the aid of the Fera? Are they offering to open their caerns? Are they offering to give positions in Caerns to other Fera? Does Albrecht expect to be head of this Alliance? What happens when a garou kills a Fera? What happens when a Fera Kills a Garou? What are the garou demanding of the fera for this alliance? No punching? Free Res' for silver Fangs? Are they pushing for multi breed packs?<br /> <br /> Or is it a simple mutual defense pact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T15:13:32-07:00","id":1100977,"title":"","content":"In addition to apologizing for the War of Rage, I think that the Western Garou would have to open their Caerns and give payment (in fetishes and talens) in symbolic compensation to the Western Fera. Giving Western Garou Kinfolk as hostages for the good behavior of the Western Garou would probably not be unwarranted. The Uktenu and the Wendigo would probably be exempt because of their historically good (or at least neutral) ties with the Western Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T15:27:34-07:00","id":1100983,"title":"","content":"I am not seeing Garou, or any fera giving up king folk as hostages, closest I see is adopting each other's kinfolk, so children of Gaia and bonegnawer taking and giving mates with the other fera.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1100876-a-peace-treaty-with-the-fera?p=1100974#post1100974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are Kitsune in the Ahdi Kitsune go where Kitsune go.<br /> <br /> <br /> More seriously rather than a vague &amp;quot;everyone fights together against problems&amp;quot;(which seems to generally have been the case in places like the Amazon) what are the specifics? What are the Garou offering for the aid of the Fera? Are they offering to open their caerns? Are they offering to give positions in Caerns to other Fera? Does Albrecht expect to be head of this Alliance? What happens when a garou kills a Fera? What happens when a Fera Kills a Garou? What are the garou demanding of the fera for this alliance? No punching? Free Res' for silver Fangs? Are they pushing for multi breed packs?<br /> <br /> Or is it a simple mutual defense pact?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see it is as Garou asking for FERA Aid and more offering FERA aid.<br /> <br /> It's much more likely if they start small and get a few septa on board by things like successfully offering asylum to Gurahl and inbetweener Rokea. Permitting more Corax assess beyond just the Fenrir, Fianna, Child of Gaia, Pure One pacts ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T15:51:20-07:00","id":1100994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1100876-a-peace-treaty-with-the-fera?p=1100974#post1100974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are Kitsune in the Ahdi Kitsune go where Kitsune go.<br /> <br /> More seriously rather than a vague &quot;everyone fights together against problems&quot;(which seems to generally have been the case in places like the Amazon) what are the specifics? What are the Garou offering for the aid of the Fera? Are they offering to open their caerns? Are they offering to give positions in Caerns to other Fera? Does Albrecht expect to be head of this Alliance? What happens when a garou kills a Fera? What happens when a Fera Kills a Garou? What are the garou demanding of the fera for this alliance? No punching? Free Res' for silver Fangs? Are they pushing for multi breed packs?<br /> <br /> Or is it a simple mutual defense pact?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much what I created the thread for. Trying to work out specifics for the meeting and the players to influence or not.<br /> <br /> What the grievances are, any sort of conditions each imposes, and so on.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I as the ST don't believe the Garou are completely at fault in the War of Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-06-2017, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T17:10:59-07:00","id":1101026,"title":"","content":"Cultural myths are more real than any history. Whether the Fera started it they generally have fewer resources than the united Garou. So they are going to likely demand some sort of reconpensation for slights real or imagined. You will likely have to have different treaties worked out by Changing Breed or by tribe of said breed(Fucking Bastet) with Corax being the easiest and Ratkin or Rokea being the hardest(Nagah are off the table, Ratkin and Rokea are barely on the table). So you have options decide which Fera you want to deal with first and don't feel pressured to bring them all in, even success might turn around those have rejected it.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking you will have people trying to use the sudden closeness to finally get revenge for some historical slight. You will also have profound misunderstandings as the various changing Breeds do not share renown and have various physeological and spiritual diferences. This will of course lead to &quot;teach us your cool secrets&quot; which will go over as well as you'd expect. I'd give a tribal break down but really what is given up will more be on a sept by sept basis there may be COGies who won't give up their sept because they know best and Shadowlords who's ruthless pragmatism says &quot;I don't care if you use our caern just don't weaken it&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T19:40:25-07:00","id":1101086,"title":"","content":"You need a common enemy and a lynch pin. For the Court it was the Keui-Jin and the Kitsune. For the Ahadi it was the Endless Storm and the Ajaba. You need to create an immediate big bad that no one breed can defeat on their own. I say immediate because the Wyrm doesn't count. The Wyrm is patient and each breed is already lulled into a false sense of security that they have time to solve that problem. You need something that threatens moving the Wyrms time table up in the here and now. Once you have that you need to have one side step up and say, &quot;Ok, shit hit the fan. Ready to talk now?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have run a story line like this before. Its a lot of fun. Just make sure to have failures otherwise is just seems to easy and your players a likely to blow it up. Hindsight... lol<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T08:52:27-07:00","id":1101252,"title":"","content":"I've got some general specifics going on here as ideas:<br /> <br /> 1. The Garou Nation and Fera will agree to a non-aggression pact within North America as well as mutual defense against attack by Wyrm creatures plus any member who doesn't want to play by their rules. They will also punish those who attack each other without cause (which gets complicated).<br /> <br /> 2. There's going to a ceremonial exchange of fetishes and apology from Albretch regarding the War of Rage plus the ceding of a token number of caerns (minor ones) which once belonged to the Fera. I'm thinking this is going to be the real issue because I think Albretch worked on smoothing things with the Wendigo before but some of their caerns originally belonged to Fera because history is just like that.<br /> <br /> 3. There will be the option for Fera to be unmolested as associates of packs and vice versa but both sides think this is mostly a personal thing anyway.<br /> <br /> 4. Both sides can call upon the other during times of war but the other side isn't necessarily supposed to answer.<br /> <br /> 5. This doesn't effect any Garou or Fera in continents other than them.<br /> <br /> Neither side thinks this is much but it's as much as they think they can get away with now. It's also something which really offends a lot of people because quite a few Garou and Fera think the wounds from the War are still fresh.<br /> <br /> They're going to be uniting against the Under the Blood Red Moon events which will be their first sign if they can do anything together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T06:09:35-07:00","id":1110811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1100876-a-peace-treaty-with-the-fera?p=1101086#post1101086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need a common enemy and a lynch pin. For the Court it was the Keui-Jin and the Kitsune. For the Ahadi it was the Endless Storm and the Ajaba. You need to create an immediate big bad that no one breed can defeat on their own. I say immediate because the Wyrm doesn't count. The Wyrm is patient and each breed is already lulled into a false sense of security that they have time to solve that problem. You need something that threatens moving the Wyrms time table up in the here and now. Once you have that you need to have one side step up and say, &quot;Ok, shit hit the fan. Ready to talk now?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have run a story line like this before. Its a lot of fun. Just make sure to have failures otherwise is just seems to easy and your players a likely to blow it up. Hindsight... lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehm.... Correction! The Kitsune are NOT the common enemy or Lynch pin of the beast courts - They are actually the glue that keeps the beastcourts rolling after the okuma (Gurahl) died out in the war of shame. Since then they keep the individual courts from falling apart, directing the wrath at the common enemies of the beast courts: the Kumo, the Technocracy, <i>invading western Garou</i> and the Kin-jin (aka: western vampires). The situation towards the Kuei-jin and eastern tradition mages is some kind of very very unstable truce with a lot of infighting and breaking of it from either side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","user":"Hira Akigi","date":". 07-09-2017, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:18:40-07:00","id":1110837,"title":"","content":"Yes. The KJ are civilized enemies of the Beast Courts while the rest of the bunch are the barbaric enemies of the Beast Courts. The Kitsune are the thread that keep the Beast Courts together because they are the depositories of the lore and magic of the Beast Courts (and the mortal lore and the mortal magic known by the Beast Courts). Remember, Rank Five Kitsune possess a potential lifespan of up to 1600 years (the equivalent of 100 years for a mortal), so they have centuries to learn every Gift, Path, Rite, and Ritual known by the Beast Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}